WEBVTT

00:00:04.799 --> 00:00:09.120
announcing [music] the arrival of His

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.719
Excellency Ferdinand R. Marcos Jr.,

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:13.679
President of the Republic of the [music]

00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:15.679
Philippines, and Honorable Donald J.

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:18.320
Trump, President of [music] the United

00:00:15.679 --> 00:00:23.000
States of America, together with First

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:23.000
Lady Louise Aronetta Marcos.

00:00:25.119 --> 00:00:28.119
Heat. Heat.

00:00:54.365 --> 00:00:56.385
>> [music]

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:12.920
>> Ladies and [music] gentlemen, please be

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:12.920
seated.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:34.640
May we invite his excellency Ferdinand

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:36.640
R. Marcos Jr. to deliver his remarks.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:38.880
>> Mr. President, distinguished guests,

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:41.439
ladies and gentlemen, it is a great

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:43.920
pleasure to welcome President Donald J.

00:01:41.439 --> 00:01:46.560
Trump back to the Philippines to host a

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:48.159
state lunchon in his honor. Mr.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:51.040
President, we are very pleased to have

00:01:48.159 --> 00:01:53.360
you with us once again. Your visit comes

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:54.880
at a particularly meaningful time as the

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:57.119
Philippines and the United States

00:01:54.880 --> 00:02:00.000
commemorate 80 years of diplomatic

00:01:57.119 --> 00:02:03.280
relations and 75 years of our alliance

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:05.040
under the mutual defense treaty. These

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:07.040
anniversaries remind us that the

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.280
relationship between our two countries

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:12.160
is not only one of governments and

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:16.000
institutions. It is also a relationship

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:18.319
between peoples built over generations.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:21.520
Strengthened by shared sacrifice,

00:02:18.319 --> 00:02:24.879
enduring friendships, family ties, and a

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:27.120
deep sense of familiarity and trust,

00:02:24.879 --> 00:02:28.959
Filipinos and Americans have stood side

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:31.040
by side through some of the most

00:02:28.959 --> 00:02:34.160
consequential moments in our shared

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:36.879
history. That bond has endured because

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:38.959
it has continued to grow and adapt with

00:02:36.879 --> 00:02:41.599
each generation.

00:02:38.959 --> 00:02:44.400
Today, we celebrate that history, but we

00:02:41.599 --> 00:02:46.800
also look ahead with optimism. Our

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:49.440
partnership today extends well beyond

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:52.560
defense and security. We are building

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:54.720
stronger ties in trade, investment, in

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:57.440
energy, in technology, resilient supply

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:59.360
chains, education, many other areas that

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:02.800
directly affect the lives and the

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:05.120
aspirations of both our peoples. Mr.

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:08.560
President, the Philippines deeply values

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:12.400
the United States as a trusted friend, a

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:14.560
steadfast partner, and an enduring ally.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:16.239
We also value the personal engagement

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:18.480
and commitment that you have brought to

00:03:16.239 --> 00:03:21.440
our relationship, ensuring that both our

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:23.360
peoples are safer, stronger, and more

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:25.760
prosperous.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:27.840
I'm confident that your visit will give

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:29.760
fresh momentum to our partnership and

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:32.080
open new opportunities for our two

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:34.720
countries to work even more closely

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:37.200
together for our peoples, for our

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:41.120
region, for the peace and prosperity

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:43.760
that we all seek. Mr. President, on

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:46.239
behalf of the people of the Philippines,

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:48.720
I extend to you once again our warmest

00:03:46.239 --> 00:03:51.440
welcome. We hope you feel very much at

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:53.680
home here in the Philippines. May I now

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:55.680
invite everyone to raise their glasses

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:58.080
to the good health and success of

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:00.799
President Trump, to the enduring

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:05.200
friendship between Filipino and American

00:04:00.799 --> 00:04:07.680
peoples, to an even stronger and dynamic

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:09.599
Philippines United alliance in the years

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:12.599
ahead.

00:04:09.599 --> 00:04:12.599
Filipinos.

00:04:13.439 --> 00:04:17.159
Cheers, sir.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:32.080
>> May we now invite the Honorable Donald

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:33.840
J. Trump to deliver his remarks.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:37.120
>> Well, thank you very much. It's a great

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:39.440
honor to be here. President Marcus,

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:41.360
Madame First Lady, thank you for your

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:42.880
magnificent welcome back to this

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:44.720
exceptionally

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:47.919
beautiful country. It really is. It's a

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:49.280
beautiful place and a lot of people are

00:04:47.919 --> 00:04:51.040
watching what's happening today and

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:54.000
they'll be coming here. This is a place

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:55.919
of great opportunity and potential.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:58.560
It's a special honor to visit you here

00:04:55.919 --> 00:05:00.960
within the walls of this storied palace

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:03.600
where some of the greatest Filipino and

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:05.280
American heroes before us have walked

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:07.280
and worked together to defend the

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:10.639
freedom and glory of both of our

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:13.840
countries. It's got tremendous history

00:05:10.639 --> 00:05:16.160
behind it. I got a tour by the president

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:17.759
and it was quite something. The bond

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:20.800
between the United States and the

00:05:17.759 --> 00:05:24.240
Philippines is cherished and unique. And

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:26.880
the alliance that we have, and it's born

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:28.960
out of a shared love of liberty was

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:32.400
proven across the generations, tempered

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:34.960
in the fine battle and sustained by a

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:37.840
mutual commitment to prosperity and

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:39.360
peace for all of our people. And we've

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:41.199
worked together beautifully. And we're

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:43.759
working together better now than ever

00:05:41.199 --> 00:05:45.280
before. And we've just consummated a

00:05:43.759 --> 00:05:48.880
very big trade deal, the biggest trade

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:50.639
deal we've ever made by far. And it's a

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:54.320
fair deal for both countries. And we're

00:05:50.639 --> 00:05:55.520
very happy with it. And uh we didn't

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:57.919
know that that was going to take place,

00:05:55.520 --> 00:06:00.960
but it took place very quickly. And it's

00:05:57.919 --> 00:06:03.039
a magnificent deal for both. So today,

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:05.759
under the leadership of President Marcus

00:06:03.039 --> 00:06:07.840
and myself, I'm proud to say that we're

00:06:05.759 --> 00:06:09.919
making the alliance between the United

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:12.319
States and the Philippines much stronger

00:06:09.919 --> 00:06:14.639
than it's ever been before, especially

00:06:12.319 --> 00:06:16.800
with the consummation of this deal.

00:06:14.639 --> 00:06:18.800
Generations ago, America ended the

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:21.360
Spanish tyranny and domination of these

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:23.039
islands and quickly laid the foundations

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:26.000
for a modern and independent

00:06:23.039 --> 00:06:27.840
Philippines. From William Howard Taft to

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:30.800
Dwight D. Eisenhower, some of the best

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:34.319
minds and foremost leaders of our nation

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:36.000
and that our nation has ever produced

00:06:34.319 --> 00:06:38.319
have just poured their hearts and their

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:40.800
souls. They always knew that this was a

00:06:38.319 --> 00:06:42.720
place of great potential. We've had a

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.919
lot of presidents look upon it, but I

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:46.479
don't think there's ever been a time

00:06:43.919 --> 00:06:49.600
like this, frankly. And of course, it

00:06:46.479 --> 00:06:52.240
was right here, this very palace that

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:55.759
President Quaison bestowed General

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:58.000
Douglas MacArthur with a gold baton and

00:06:55.759 --> 00:06:59.759
the rank of field marshal in the

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:02.319
Philippine Army. I'd like to have you do

00:06:59.759 --> 00:07:04.000
that to me if you don't mind. I love

00:07:02.319 --> 00:07:07.280
that. I mean, why the hell shouldn't I

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:10.720
get that? But to help prepare the proud

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:13.039
nation to defend the land and really the

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:15.120
land of their fathers. And when the

00:07:13.039 --> 00:07:20.080
battle came from the streets of Manila

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:23.440
to the steep cliffs of Corridor to the

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:25.840
immortal heroes of Baton, brave American

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:28.560
and Filipino sons shed their blood into

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:31.680
the same sand, rock and mud to defend

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:34.880
this land and the land of our brothers

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:36.479
and our sisters and our mothers, our

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:40.319
fathers.

00:07:36.479 --> 00:07:42.560
260,000 Philippine heroes fought beneath

00:07:40.319 --> 00:07:44.639
the stars and stripes of World War II

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:47.360
and countless American service members

00:07:44.639 --> 00:07:50.960
gave their lives to fulfill that famous

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:54.080
pledge of MacArthur. I shall return. He

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:56.000
said, I shall return. because of the

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:59.520
sacrifice of those who gave everything

00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:02.080
to keep that vow. Today, the Philippines

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:04.560
are free and Manila is home to the

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:06.479
largest overseas American military

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:09.039
cemetery anywhere in the world. Many

00:08:06.479 --> 00:08:10.720
people died defending the Philippines

00:08:09.039 --> 00:08:13.599
and that's why I'm so happy that we were

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:16.240
able to do a deal today. This is the

00:08:13.599 --> 00:08:19.759
kind of history that binds nations

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:22.560
forever. And today we really uh we look

00:08:19.759 --> 00:08:25.440
to those before us. President Marcos and

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:28.240
I continue to work to defend the peace

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:31.919
our ancestors won and they so bravely

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:37.360
won. The the level of hardship, the lab

00:08:31.919 --> 00:08:40.000
level of terror and the level of love in

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:42.240
this country has been extraordinary. And

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:43.839
the freedom our children will inherit

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:46.480
for generations to come. and they'll

00:08:43.839 --> 00:08:48.320
look to the Philippines as just a very

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:51.600
important place even in American

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:54.800
history. And now it becomes with today's

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:57.839
deal, it becomes more important and more

00:08:54.800 --> 00:09:00.160
united. Our two nations along with Japan

00:08:57.839 --> 00:09:02.959
recently launched the Luzon Economic

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:05.760
Guard to facilitate critically needed

00:09:02.959 --> 00:09:08.080
infrastructure in the central crossroads

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:10.480
of the world. And this year we're

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:13.519
celebrating the 75th anniversary of our

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:15.600
mutual defense agreement which we marked

00:09:13.519 --> 00:09:17.760
by conducting our largest ever joint

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:21.440
exercise bringing together all of our

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:23.120
forces across air, land, sea, cyber, and

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:25.519
space.

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:28.640
Although we are separated by thousands

00:09:25.519 --> 00:09:31.120
of miles, and when I say thousands, it's

00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:33.760
thousands and thousands of miles far

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:35.600
away, but it really seems close to me

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:37.440
because of the relationship. It doesn't

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:40.800
seem far away, but our countries are

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:43.680
still united by common interests and by

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:45.760
the even more enduring ties of culture

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:48.959
and commerce and the values that first

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:51.600
brought us together so long ago. And as

00:09:48.959 --> 00:09:53.760
we can see in the beautiful Christmas

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:56.080
decorations and Christmas is such a big

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:58.800
part of the Philippines. I came and I

00:09:56.080 --> 00:10:00.399
said, "Wow, that's really something."

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:01.839
They didn't talk about taking Christmas

00:10:00.399 --> 00:10:04.399
away. You know, in our country, they

00:10:01.839 --> 00:10:08.320
said, "Let's not use Christmas anymore."

00:10:04.399 --> 00:10:10.320
In 2016, we ended that. That was ended.

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:12.000
But they treat they treat Christmas with

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:13.920
great love and respect in the

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:16.880
Philippines. Decorations displayed

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:21.760
throughout this palace and all of Manila

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:26.000
show that our people are also united by

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:28.560
faith in God and uh the Filipinos are

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:30.880
with us all the way. Religion, religion

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:33.200
is a very big part of the Philippines.

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:36.000
So, President Marcos and Madame First

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:38.079
Lady, two incredible people. Thank you

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:40.640
again for your extraordinary welcome and

00:10:38.079 --> 00:10:44.000
continued friendship. And I ask everyone

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:47.760
to please join me in raising a toast.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:49.839
May our alliance stand as strong as the

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:51.760
heroes who forged it. And together, may

00:10:49.839 --> 00:10:54.399
we lead the United States and the

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:56.800
Philippines toward a future of even

00:10:54.399 --> 00:10:58.720
greater safety, prosperity, and peace.

00:10:56.800 --> 00:11:00.399
These are wonderful people. This is a

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:01.920
wonderful place and it's an honor to be

00:11:00.399 --> 00:11:02.560
here. Thank you very much.

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:03.680
>> Thank you very much.

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:07.320
>> Thank you very much.

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:07.320
>> Thank you. Cheers, sir.

00:11:08.399 --> 00:11:12.680
>> Thank you. Thank you very much.

00:11:19.839 --> 00:11:23.920
Thank you, your excellencies,

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:25.680
distinguished guests, ladies and

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:28.680
gentlemen, we shall now begin the

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:28.680
lunchon.
